# The step of the map add_1 on arrays that the program supplies (milestone2.md, "Arrays that the
# program fills"): both operands pass through guard, rule R3, then add_1_1. Its claims are those
# of add_1_1.
kernel:        add_entry_step_1
input:         x
input:         y
output:        z
value:         x+y
ensures:       rounded z nearest
ensures:       error z R c=1/(1+u) k=1 t=0
min_precision: 1
theorem:       proofs/theories/MapSteps.v add_entry_step_1_correct
source:        add_1_1 on guarded operands (rule R3); one rounding to nearest
license:       bound: published; proof: MIT
status:        proved
entry:         yes
ieee:          bridge

gx = guard(x)
gy = guard(y)
z  = add_1_1(gx, gy)
